---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ReconExplainer from '../components/ReconExplainer.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<Base
	title="Finding data that didn't arrive"
	description="An interactive walk-through of a cross-instance reconciliation proof of concept: fingerprint, classify drift both ways, drill down to the keys."
>
	<article>
		<p class="eyebrow">Proof of concept · cross-instance reconciliation</p>
		<h1>Finding data that didn't arrive</h1>
		<p class="lede">
			Replication rarely fails loudly. A row goes missing, or a delete never lands, and every system still looks healthy. This
			proof of concept is a read-only engine in ksh and SQL. It fingerprints each table and company code (row count plus key
			hash, over all rows and over the last 30 days), compares three Oracle instances, and classifies drift in both directions,
			with a drill-down HTML dashboard.
		</p>
		<p class="note">
			It is a working proof of concept, in use for validation. The instances, table and rows below are invented; the
			hashes are real SHA-1 prefixes of the invented keys.
		</p>

		<h2>Step through it</h2>
		<ReconExplainer />

		<h2>What it found for real</h2>
		<ul class="found">
			<li>It caught a flawed key heuristic before that heuristic produced false drift.</li>
			<li>It surfaced stale rows left behind by deletes that never propagated: rows still in a target after the source deleted them.</li>
		</ul>

		<p class="limit">
			<strong>Honest limit:</strong> Fingerprints cover row counts and key hashes, so they find missing and stale rows. A row whose
			key landed but whose values didn't would pass; catching that needs a value hash too.
		</p>

		<p class="back"><a class="btn press" href={url('projects/')}>← Projects</a> <a class="btn press" href={url()}>The pipeline</a></p>
	</article>
</Base>

<style>
	h1 {
		max-width: var(--measure);
		margin-block: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
	}
	p,
	.found {
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}
	.note {
		margin-bottom: 3rem;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	h2 {
		margin-block: 3.5rem 1rem;
	}
	.found {
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}
	.found li + li {
		margin-top: 0.4rem;
	}
	.limit {
		margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
		padding: 0.875rem 1.125rem;
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		background: var(--error-bg);
		box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 var(--error);
	}
	.back {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.625rem;
		margin-top: 3.5rem;
	}
</style>
